        "code": "# The 00- prefix makes this file the FIRST one read: for each keyword,\n# sshd keeps the first value it finds, so nothing can override these lines.\n\n# --- Who may log in ------------------------------------------------\n# root never logs in directly: use a personal account, then sudo\nPermitRootLogin no\n# Only members of this group may open a session\nAllowGroups ssh-users\n\n# --- How they authenticate -----------------------------------------\n# Keys only: no password can be guessed, reused or phished\nPubkeyAuthentication yes\nPasswordAuthentication no\nKbdInteractiveAuthentication no\nPermitEmptyPasswords no\nAuthenticationMethods publickey\n\n# --- Limit abuse ---------------------------------------------------\nMaxAuthTries 3\nMaxSessions 4\nLoginGraceTime 30\n# Close sessions that have been dead for 10 minutes (2 x 300 s)\nClientAliveInterval 300\nClientAliveCountMax 2\n\n# --- Reduce features -----------------------------------------------\n# The server is not a tunnel, a proxy or an X11 display\nX11Forwarding no\nAllowTcpForwarding no\nAllowAgentForwarding no\nPermitTunnel no\nPermitUserEnvironment no\n\n# --- Logging -------------------------------------------------------\n# VERBOSE records the fingerprint of the key used at each login\nLogLevel VERBOSE\n\n# --- Cryptography (check your version with: ssh -Q kex) ------------\nKexAlgorithms sntrup761x25519-sha512@openssh.com,curve25519-sha256,curve25519-sha256@libssh.org\nCiphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com,aes128-gcm@openssh.com\nMACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com\nHostKeyAlgorithms ssh-ed25519,rsa-sha2-512,rsa-sha2-256\n",
