        "en": "You inherit an Ubuntu server whose `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` file contains:\n\n```text\nPermitRootLogin yes\nPasswordAuthentication yes\nMaxAuthTries 6\nX11Forwarding yes\n```\n\nYour `alice` account already has a public key in `~/.ssh/authorized_keys`.\n\nWrite a script that:\n\n1. creates the `ssh-users` group and adds `alice` to it;\n2. writes a `/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardening.conf` file that forbids `root`, passwords and X11\n   forwarding, limits attempts to 3 and only allows the `ssh-users` group;\n3. validates the configuration and reloads the service **only** if it is correct;\n4. prints the effective values of those five directives.\n"
